WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.009 --> 00:00:00.639
Example,

1
00:00:00.889 --> 00:00:02.660
using the local storage hook.

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.670
Here is an example of how to use the use local storage custom hook

3
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.409
inside a react component.

4
00:00:09.119 --> 00:00:11.060
This component manages a user's name,

5
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:12.800
stores it in local storage,

6
00:00:13.039 --> 00:00:15.119
and retrieves it after a page reload.

7
00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:18.229
Let's do it.

8
00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:19.569
First,

9
00:00:19.809 --> 00:00:22.489
declare a state variable using the custom hook.

10
00:00:23.049 --> 00:00:23.530
Type

11
00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:24.469
const,

12
00:00:24.729 --> 00:00:25.170
name,

13
00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:26.200
set name

14
00:00:26.409 --> 00:00:27.110
equals

15
00:00:27.409 --> 00:00:28.729
use local storage.

16
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.620
Pass username as the key

17
00:00:31.879 --> 00:00:34.299
and an empty string as the initial value.

18
00:00:34.959 --> 00:00:37.340
Don't forget to import use local storage

19
00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:40.639
and make sure it is exported properly from the custom hook file.

20
00:00:45.729 --> 00:00:46.220
Now,

21
00:00:46.689 --> 00:00:48.029
inside the return statement,

22
00:00:48.369 --> 00:00:49.849
display a welcome message.

23
00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:51.659
If name exists,

24
00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:53.610
display welcome name.

25
00:00:54.069 --> 00:00:54.490
Otherwise,

26
00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.310
display welcome guest.

27
00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:57.549
Next,

28
00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:58.919
add an input field.

29
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:01.770
Set the input's value to name.

30
00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:02.939
For on change,

31
00:01:03.169 --> 00:01:05.260
use an arrow function to update the name.

32
00:01:05.849 --> 00:01:06.489
Type

33
00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:10.129
set name event.target.value.

34
00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:11.529
Now,

35
00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.470
add a button to clear the stored name.

36
00:01:14.129 --> 00:01:14.790
When clicked,

37
00:01:14.889 --> 00:01:17.089
it should remove the item from local storage.

38
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.919
Let's see it in action.

39
00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:20.029
Here,

40
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.769
we can see the name stored in local storage.

41
00:01:23.529 --> 00:01:23.790
Now,

42
00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:28.269
let's open the browser's developer tools and go to the application tab.

43
00:01:28.989 --> 00:01:29.870
In local storage,

44
00:01:29.949 --> 00:01:31.430
we can see the stored name.

45
00:01:32.139 --> 00:01:34.319
If we change the name and reload the page,

46
00:01:34.739 --> 00:01:36.080
the updated name is still there.

47
00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.839
That's how we use the use local storage hook.

48
00:01:57.959 --> 00:01:59.319
See you in the next lesson.